            <ArticleTitle>Ectopic gastric mucosa presenting as a polypoid mass within a Meckel's diverticulum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>585-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 32-year-old man presented with severe abdominal pain located in the mesogastrium and right hemi-abdomen. A barium transit study showed a tubular structure of 6 cm arising from a bowel loop in the distal ileum, with an intraluminal polypoid mass near the bottom. Diagnosis of a benign lesion within a Meckel's diverticulum was made. Anatomopathology confirmed a Meckel's diverticulum and demonstrated that the polypoid mass was caused by an unusual great ectopic island of gastric mucosa.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
